  "summary": "The aesthetic tradition of using pure white or blue-gray marble from the Carrara quarries in Tuscany.",
  "description": "Characterized by its fine grain and subtle gray veining on a pure white background, valued since antiquity for sculpture and architecture. The aesthetic emerged from the unique geological properties of the Apuan Alps and the region's marble-working heritage.",
